<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="seq" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="flow_id" attr.type="long" />
  <key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="service" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="graph" attr.name="graph_usable" attr.type="boolean" />
  <key id="d3" for="graph" attr.name="categories" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d2" for="graph" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="link" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">Techwood / CNN Center (Atlanta on-prem)</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyDataStream</data>
      <data key="d7">Linear Ops QCs the master files in Atlanta and sends them to the cloud via Aspera. Receives the cloud playout back as a unicast signal, then compresses it and brings it to the uplink. An on-site auto changeover switch selects between Techwood playout, CNN Center playout and cloud playout. The cloud path is the 'X chain', a tertiary path to air. Evertz CloudBridge bookends the connection on site.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">S3 master file storage</data>
      <data key="d6">S3</data>
      <data key="d7">Stores all master files for all brands. Files are registered in Evertz Mediator before being transferred to EC2.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">EC2 playout (Evertz ORT)</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">Runs Evertz ORT software; files are played out using Evertz Playtime. 10 channels per AZ in us-east-1 (30 channels total), each channel with a primary and a backup. Instances are supported by Auto Scaling groups. Multi-AZ redundancy targets five-nines availability. Evertz CloudBridge carries the signal from the ORT back to site.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">Direct Connect</data>
      <data key="d6">DirectConnect</data>
      <data key="d7">Carries the playout back to prem as a unicast signal (X chain to Atlanta). For the BCP solution it also goes to Hudson Yards in New York (8 channels). Evertz CloudBridge runs in AWS, Atlanta and New York.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">Uplink (ATL / NYC)</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyEdge</data>
      <data key="d7">Uplink for distribution to affiliates. The Atlanta uplink is fed with the compressed signal from the on-prem site; the NYC uplink is fed by the BCP path through Hudson Yards (8 channels).</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="1" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">QC'd master files are sent from Atlanta to S3 via Aspera.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Signal is compressed and brought to the uplink for distribution to affiliates.</data>
      <data key="d10">4</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once registered in Evertz Mediator, files are transferred to the local EC2 running Evertz ORT.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Playout from Evertz Playtime goes out via Direct Connect, using Evertz CloudBridge.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="0" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Playout returns to prem as a unicast signal (the X chain, a tertiary path to air).</data>
      <data key="d10">3</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">WarnerMedia HBO Cloud Linear Playout</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMK2NJ-q9nc</data>
    <data key="d2">Cloud linear playout for WarnerMedia HBO in AWS us-east-1. It started as a business continuity (BCP) solution and grew to support 30 channels. Evertz software (Mediator, ORT, Playtime, CloudBridge) runs on EC2 across multiple AZs, targeting five-nines availability. CloudFormation (about 40 scrubbed YAML templates) was used only to make deployment repeatable and is omitted as a non-runtime layer. Future plans: live venue inputs switched with pre-recorded content on the ORT, and muxing/compression in the cloud for direct handoff to an MVPD.</data>
    <data key="d3">Media &amp; Entertainment, Linear Playout, Business Continuity, Hybrid Connectivity</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
